# Mercury Edit 2 — findings by MiniMax M3.1 Flash

- Source: Inception (mercury-edit-2)
- Date: 2026-11-12 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Mercury Edit 2
- **Short description:** Inception Labs' purpose-built diffusion LLM (dLLM) for **next-edit prediction and fill-in-the-middle code completion** — an editor-side specialist that predicts the developer's next code change from recent snippets, the current file and the edit history, and is aligned to human accept/reject preferences with KTO. Not a general chat model: it has no chat endpoint, no reasoning control and no tool calling, so it must be judged as a code-editing component, not as an assistant.
- **Provider / access:** Inception API only, on two dedicated endpoints — `POST https://api.inceptionlabs.ai/v1/fim/completions` (inline autocomplete with a prefix and optional suffix) and `POST https://api.inceptionlabs.ai/v1/edit/completions` (next-edit suggestion built from recently viewed snippets, the current file with an editable region, and a time-ordered unidiff edit history). Model id `mercury-edit-2`. Not listed on OpenRouter, and there is no OpenCode Zen route — the OpenCode Console catalog lists no Mercury model.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-03-30 (Inception blog index date; models.dev release date 2026-03-30). Knowledge cutoff not disclosed.
- **IDs:** `inception/mercury-edit-2` (models.dev canonical id); `mercury-edit-2` (Inception API). No free Zen ID exists.
- **Context window:** 32,000 tokens for both the FIM and the Next-Edit endpoints, with 8,192 max output tokens — verified on the Inception models-and-pricing doc and the models.dev model record. (BenchLM's model page instead lists 128K; see the conflict section.)
- **Modalities:** text in / text out only. Reasoning: no — BenchLM classifies it as a non-reasoning model and models.dev records reasoning as unsupported. Tool calling: no (the FIM endpoint explicitly does not support tool or function calling). Structured outputs: no. Temperature control: yes.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-12):** $0.25 per 1M input tokens and $0.75 per 1M output tokens, cached input $0.025 per 1M. Paid model, with a time-limited allowance of 10 million free tokens automatically granted to every new Inception API account; Zed users could unlock one free month of edit suggestions with a vendor-issued key.
- **Architecture:** proprietary diffusion LLM trained for edit prediction; trained on a curated multi-language edit dataset and then preference-aligned with Kahneman-Tversky Optimization (KTO), an unpaired reinforcement-learning method, using recorded accept/reject feedback. Parameter count not disclosed.

